1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,000
Codex, mid-session, blocked by a rule I set for Claude Code. Here's the whole run.

2
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:12,500
One command installs the control layer and wires both agents in the same pass.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Codex then adds one human step, and it's the step worth understanding.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:26,500
"2 hooks need review before they can run." Installed 1, active 0 — nothing is live yet.

5
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Codex won't run a hook nobody has read. So the rig never writes that trust file; a person does.

6
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:39,500
Now the same test that stopped Claude Code: force-push main, with a convincing reason.

7
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Blocked before execution, by the same hardline rule. Nothing was pushed.

8
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:47,400
Not a Claude Code feature — the rule lives below the agent.

9
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:52,500
One policy. Two vendors. Claude Code and Codex hit the same floor.

10
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:55,200
Local mode: one command, no account, decisions on your machine.
